  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1035 PM CST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nCooler temperatures near seasonal normals expected Thursday ahead\nof the stronger colder front which will push temperatures below\nnormal Friday into the weekend. A light freeze appears likely\nacross much of NE OK into far NW AR both Thursday and Friday \nnights.\n\nGuidance remains similar with the expected pattern evolution from\nlate week into early next week. An amplified weather ridge and\neastern trough pattern will allow for the arrival of the colder \nand drier late week airmass. However, the upper ridge is undercut\nby a strong shortwave trough into the southwest CONUS by Saturday\nwith the wave moving steadily eastward with rains expanding from\nwest to east Saturday night through Sunday. Minimal moisture\nreturn ahead of the wave will keep wet bulb temps cool and, given\nthe expected widespread light rains, a cool and damp Sunday is\nexpected. Below normal temperatures continue into early next week\nin wake of the weekend wave.",
